# Range loop promotes the iteration value at an integer boundary

Verifies an `int8` loop variable widens to `int16` after its maximum value so
an end-exclusive `int16` bound remains reachable without repeating or
overflowing an iteration value.

>>> source
start: int8 = 126
end: int16 = 130
for (index in start..end) {
    print(index)
}

<<< stdout
126
127
128
129

<<< stderr
